Install the [AWS CLI v2](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/userguide/getting-started-install.html), sign in with a named profile (any name works, `{{projectName}}` here) and choose the region. `AWS_PROFILE` and `AWS_REGION` are the only places the profile and the region are set: no file of the project names them, and in CI the OIDC step provides the credentials and `AWS_REGION`.

```bash
aws configure sso --profile {{projectName}}
aws sso login --profile {{projectName}}
export AWS_PROFILE="{{projectName}}"
export AWS_REGION=eu-west-3
aws sts get-caller-identity
```

Replace `eu-west-3` with your region. For an IAM user's access key, run `aws configure --profile {{projectName}}` instead of the first two commands. `aws sts get-caller-identity` must print the account you mean to deploy to. The two `export` lines last for the terminal session: set them again in each new one.
